=== HINT 1: Connect ===
int conn = connect(s, (struct sockaddr*)&addr, sizeof(addr));

=== HINT 2: Set receive timeout ===
DWORD timeout_ms = 2000;
setsockopt(s, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVTIMEO, (char*)&timeout_ms, sizeof(timeout_ms));

=== HINT 3: Send probe, then read banner ===
if (send_str) send(s, send_str, (int)strlen(send_str), 0);
int n = recv(s, buf, sizeof(buf)-1, 0);
buf[n > 0 ? n : 0] = '\0';
// FTP/SMTP send their banner without any probe - just recv after connect.

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
Banner grabbing reveals: software name, version, OS, misconfiguration.
HTTP Server header: "Apache/2.4.41 (Ubuntu)" or "Microsoft-IIS/10.0".
FTP 220: "220 (vsFTPd 3.0.3)" - reveals version for exploit research.
SSH: "SSH-2.0-OpenSSH_8.2p1 Ubuntu-4ubuntu0.5".
Active fingerprinting alternatives: nmap -sV (version scan), nmap NSE scripts.
Passive fingerprinting: p0f - identify OS/service from packet timing without sending.
